  "scientific_decisions": [
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        102,
        103,
        104
      ],
      "decision": "Heat is energy transfer rather than a material contained in a body. Mechanical work can change internal energy; melting need not raise temperature. Source colloquial heat/internal-energy language is clarified without introducing unsupported quantitative formulas."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        104,
        105,
        106
      ],
      "decision": "Thermal expansion is not universal over every substance/temperature. Liquid water maximum density near4°C under ordinary pressure is explicit. Bimetal refers only to depicted copper/iron pair; no arbitrary universal bending direction."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        106,
        107,
        108,
        109,
        110
      ],
      "decision": "Conduction vs bulk-flow convection vs radiation distinguished. Conductivity table is condition-dependent. Color comparison restricted to matched materials/illumination. Vacuum does not block radiation; reflective thermos surface has separate function. No hazardous heating paper/glass experiment assigned."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        110,
        111,
        112
      ],
      "decision": "Historical Ibn Sino trapped-air hypothesis is not presented as the correct modern cause of ice buoyancy. Beruniy counter-observation is an example of hypothesis testing. Insulation slows transfer and is not a heat source. No historical priority dates tested."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        112,
        113,
        114
      ],
      "decision": "Celsius boiling-water reference includes pure water/normal atmospheric pressure. Laboratory and retained-reading medical thermometer distinguished; no mercury handling or diagnosis. No universal36.6°C health rule or obsolete temperature record tested. §42 uses supplied hypothetical records, not a heat-balance/mean-temperature formula or actual experiment completion."
    }
